## What changed

**`src/env.ts` (new)** — `fromEnv(env, prefix = 'APP_')` returns `Partial<Config>`, reading `{prefix}PORT`, `{prefix}HOST`, `{prefix}DEBUG`, `{prefix}NAME`. Absent or empty values are left out. `PORT` is coerced with `Number`; a non-numeric value throws `TypeError` naming the variable (e.g. `APP_PORT must be a number, got "many"`). `DEBUG` is lowercased and matched against `true/1/yes` and `false/0/no`; anything else throws `TypeError` naming the variable. `HOST`/`NAME` stay strings.

**`src/config.ts`** — added `validate(config): Config`, which throws `TypeError` naming the field when `port` is not an integer in 1–65535, or when `host`/`name` is empty; otherwise returns the config unchanged.

**`src/index.ts`** — `resolveConfig(file, env = process.env)` now merges defaults ← file ← `fromEnv(env)` and runs `validate` last. The previous single-argument call keeps working.

**Tests** — new `src/env.test.ts` and `src/config.test.ts`, plus extended `src/index.test.ts` for the env-over-file precedence, `process.env` default, and validation of the merged result. `index.test.ts` cleans up `process.env` after each test so runs don't leak into one another.

